# FitnessApp Swift Architecture

## Design Tokens — Use AppStyle

Never use hardcoded styling values. Always use `AppStyle` tokens from `Shared/Design/AppStyle.swift`:

```swift
// BAD
.font(.system(size: 14, weight: .semibold))
.foregroundColor(Color(hex: "#088177"))
.padding(.horizontal, 18)
.cornerRadius(12)
.opacity(0.55)

// GOOD
.font(AppStyle.Font.tileLabel)
.foregroundColor(AppStyle.Color.green)
.padding(.horizontal, AppStyle.Padding.horizontal)
.cornerRadius(AppStyle.CornerRadius.defaultButton)
.opacity(AppStyle.Opacity.overlayBackdrop)
```

If no matching token exists, add one to `AppStyle` first, then reference it.

## Shared Components — Do Not Duplicate

Before building custom UI, check these existing components:

- `MetricChipView` — framed chip with background/stroke (cards, active sets)
- `WorkoutFormSheet` — full-screen sheet with header, drag indicator, save button
- `AnalyticsDetailSection` / `AnalyticsDetailHeader` — expandable analytics cards
- `ExercisePickerSheetModifier` / `ExercisePickerActionButtons` — bottom sheet chrome
- `ExerciseWheelPickerRow` — sets/reps/weight wheel picker row
- `ExercisePickerInputField` — styled text input for picker sheets

## Utilities — Centralized Logic

- **Weight display**: `WeightFormatter.displayWeight(_:)` — never format weights manually.
- **Analytics dates**: `AnalyticsDateHelper` — for month names, unique days, days-in-month.

## MVVM Structure

- Feature folder: `Features/<FeatureName>/`
- ViewModel: `class <Name>ViewModel: ObservableObject` with `@Published` properties
- View: `@StateObject private var viewModel` for owned ViewModels
- No business logic in Views — delegate to ViewModel or Service

## Navigation

- All destinations in `NavigationDestination` enum (`FitnessAppApp.swift`)
- Navigate via `navigationPath.append(NavigationDestination.<case>)`
- New screens require a new enum case and a `.navigationDestination` entry
